<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 182-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 182-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on 182-day Treasury</p>
<p>bills at Tuesday's auction and all of the 40 million litas</p>
<p>issue was sold as it was oversubscribed, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 11.28 percent, down from the 11.91</p>
<p>percent offered at the last auction for 182-day paper on April</p>
<p>1.</p>
<p>The settlement date is April 11 and the bills mature</p>
<p>October 10.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas with the exception of</p>
<p>yields and days.</p>
<p>SOLD  DAYS  MIN/MAX YIELD  AV.YIELD  LAST AV.YIELD  DEMAND</p>
<p>40    182   10.60/11.50	11.28     11.91	  87.734</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
